meta {
  name: Accept Consent
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/portal/consent
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: {{portalOrigin}}
  X-CSRF-Token: {{portalCsrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "accepted": true
  }
}

docs {
  Requires the server to run with `ENABLE_SELF_SERVE=true` ("Mis citas" is off by default: every
  /portal path answers 404) and a `portal_session` cookie. No login issues that cookie now that the
  codes are gone, so this request only works against a session minted for a future login.

  Records data-processing consent at the server's current privacy policy version (the client never
  sends a version). Always 204: it records a consent only for an existing patient with portal
  access, and is a no-op otherwise. Needs the session cookie, the exact Origin and the CSRF token
  from Get Session.
}
